From 16cffb6063b4afc5a4e691ac1eb55568552be646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:22:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 129/174] route: remote rule-sets can be updated on request

RuleSetUpdater.UpdateNow updates every remote rule-set at once, whatever its
update_interval, and returns how many there are, how many got a new list and
how many failed. The update runs in the updater's own goroutine, where the
scheduled ones run, so nothing of a rule-set is touched from two places; the
next scheduled update of each rule-set is counted from the forced one.
Router.UpdateRuleSets is how an embedder reaches it.

A caller that gives up, and an updater that is closed, let the call go.
